{
  "kanda": "bala",
  "sarga": 59,
  "title": "Trishanku undertakes a Vedic ritual",
  "sourceUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/baala/sarga59/balasans59.htm",
  "romanUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/baala/sarga59/balaitrans59.htm",
  "translator": "Desiraju Hanumanta Rao",
  "introduction": [
    "Vishvamitra undertakes Trishanku's Vedic ritual and sends disciples to invite all Vedic-scholars. Many sages have come except for Vashishta and his sons. Further, the sons of Vashishta have ridiculed this ritual of Vishvamitra and Trishanku. Vishvamitra gets irritated and hurls curses at the sons of Vashishta."
  ],
  "closing": [
    "इति वाल्मीकिरामायणे आदिकाव्ये बालकाण्डे एकोनषष्टितमः सर्गः",
    "Thus, this is the 59th chapter in Bala Kanda of Valmiki Ramayana, the First Epic poem of India."
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "1.59.1",
      "label": "1.59.1",
      "numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "devanagari": "उक्तवाक्यं तु राजानं कृपया कुशिकात्मजः |\nअब्रवीन्मधुरं वाक्यं साक्षाच्चण्डालतां गतम्",
      "iast": "ukta vākyam tu rājānam kṛpayā kuśika ātmajaḥ |\nabravīt madhuram vākyam sākṣāt caṇḍālatām gatam",
      "translation": "\"Vishvamitra, the son of Kushi, piteously spoke this mellowly sentence to king Trishanku who spoke thus, and who in reality attained a state of profaner.\" Thus Sage Shataananda continued his narration.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "ukta vaakyam tu",
          "iast": "ukta vākyam tu",
          "devanagari": "उक्त वाक्यं तु",
          "meaning": "spoken, word - one who spoke thus, Trishanku, but",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "saakSaat caNDaalataam gatam",
          "iast": "sākṣāt caṇḍālatām gatam",
          "devanagari": "साक्षात् चण्डालतां गतं",
          "meaning": "in reality, profaner-hood, attained one",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 10
        },
        {
          "itrans": "raajaanam",
          "iast": "rājānam",
          "devanagari": "राजानं",
          "meaning": "to king",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 3
        },
        {
          "itrans": "kR^ipayaa kushika aatmajaH",
          "iast": "kṛpayā kuśika ātmajaḥ",
          "devanagari": "कृपया कुशिक आत्मजः",
          "meaning": "piteously, Kushi's, son [Vishvamitra]",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 4
        },
        {
          "itrans": "madhuram vaakyam abraviit",
          "iast": "madhuram vākyam abravīt",
          "devanagari": "मधुरं वाक्यं अब्रवीत्",
          "meaning": "mellowly, sentence, spoke.",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 7
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1.59.2",
      "label": "1.59.2",
      "numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "devanagari": "इक्ष्वाको स्वागतं वत्स जानामि त्वां सुधार्मिकम् |\nशरणं ते भविष्यामि मा भैषीर्नृपपुंगव",
      "iast": "ikṣvāko svāgatam vatsa jānāmi tvām sudhārmikam |\nśaraṇam te bhaviṣyāmi mā bhaiṣīḥ nṛpa puṅgava",
      "translation": "\" 'Oh, Trishanku, the legatee of Ikshvaku-s, you are welcome. I am aware that you are a highly righteous king. Oh, the best king, you need not be dismayed, for I accord you haven.",
