    {
      "id": "1.59.13",
      "label": "1.59.13",
      "numbers": [
        13
      ],
      "devanagari": "क्षत्रियो याजको यस्य चण्डालस्य विशेषतः\nकथं सदसि भोक्तारो हविस्तस्य सुरर्षयः |",
      "iast": "kṣatriyo yājako yasya caṇḍālasya viśeṣataḥ\nkatham sadasi bhoktāro haviḥ tasya sura ṛṣayaḥ |",
      "translation": "\" 'A Kshatriya is the officiator, and a profaner is the performer. How then the gods or sages can partake of the remnants of oblations in that ritual-assembly, especially that of a profaner?' Thus, the sons of Vashishta exclaimed.",
      "notes": [
        "One who is uninitiated into any esoteric knowledge is venturing to perform a Vedic ritual and a king, who can perform a ritual, but who cannot officiate ritual or teach Veda-s like a Brahman, is officiating it. Thus both of these, officiator and performer have no Vedic sanctity."
      ],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "yasya",
          "iast": "yasya",
          "devanagari": "यस्य",
          "meaning": "to whom",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 2
        },
        {
          "itrans": "kSatriyaH yaajakaH",
          "iast": "kṣatriyaḥ yājakaḥ",
          "devanagari": "क्षत्रियः याजकः",
          "meaning": "a Kshatriya, officiator of ritual",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "visheSataH caNDaalasya",
          "iast": "viśeṣataḥ caṇḍālasya",
          "devanagari": "विशेषतः चण्डालस्य",
          "meaning": "especially, of a profaner",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 3
        },
        {
          "itrans": "tasya sadasi",
          "iast": "tasya sadasi",
          "devanagari": "तस्य सदसि",
          "meaning": "in such a, ritual-assembly [of a profaner]",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 6
        },
        {
          "itrans": "sura R^iSayaH",
          "iast": "sura ṛṣayaḥ",
          "devanagari": "सुर ऋषयः",
          "meaning": "gods, sages",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 10
        },
        {
          "itrans": "haviH katham bhoktaaraH",
          "iast": "haviḥ katham bhoktāraḥ",
          "devanagari": "हविः कथं भोक्तारः",
          "meaning": "oblation, how, one can partake of.",
          "anvayaIndex": 5,
          "verseIndex": 5
        }
      ]
